mesa-symbian: the Symbian port of Mesa
Copyright The Phorepoc Authors (see AUTHORS)

Phorepoc was founded by Kyriakos Bompotis.

This repository ports Mesa (https://mesa3d.org, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa) to Symbian. Mesa itself is
not copied here: build.sh fetches the version pinned in mesa.lock, and Mesa keeps its own licences (mostly MIT; see
docs/license.rst in Mesa). Thanks to the Mesa developers.

Three files are adapted from Mesa's Haiku support and keep their authors' copyright (MIT):
  symbian/src/egl_symbian.c   from src/egl/drivers/haiku/egl_haiku.cpp, Copyright (C) 2014 Adrián Arroyo Calle
  symbian/src/sym_frontend.c  from src/gallium/frontends/hgl/hgl.c, Copyright 2012-2014 Haiku, Inc.
                              (authors Artur Wyszynski, Alexander von Gluck IV)
  symbian/src/sym_winsys.c    from src/gallium/winsys/sw/hgl/hgl_sw_winsys.cpp, Copyright 2009 Artur Wyszynski,
                              Copyright 2013-2014 Alexander von Gluck IV
Thanks to the Haiku project, whose port showed the way.

Everything here is under the MIT licence (LICENSE). The Symbian headers and libraries it compiles against are the
Symbian Foundation's (EPL-1.0) and come from the Phorepoc core repository.
